Usage: zm [options] [command]

Zoom meeting transcripts and summaries

Options:
  -V, --version               output the version number
  --json                      one JSON value
  --jsonl                     one JSON object per item
  --no-input                  disable interactive login
  --interactive               permit browser approval in an interactive terminal
  --quiet                     suppress non-error diagnostics
  --fields <paths>            project result fields, such as id,title
  --timeout <duration>        command deadline: reads 30s, login 5m, downloads
                              1h; watch/MCP have no default
  --max-output-bytes <bytes>  bound rendered result bytes (default 4194304; zero
                              is unlimited)
  --offline                   refuse network requests
  -h, --help                  display help for command

Commands:
  config                      local Zoom configuration
  login [options]             log in to Zoom through your browser
  meetings                    stored meetings and their records
  pull [options]              fetch meeting records from the connected account
  import [options] <folder>   import downloaded meeting transcripts
  events                      the owner's stored events
  commands [path...]          discover commands, flags and examples, optionally
                              scoped to a command path
  complete [words...]         answer shell completion requests
  doctor                      check local runtime and public config without a
                              login or database
  session                     inspect the saved OAuth session separately from
                              local data profiles
  watch [options] [folder]    foreground serial API pulls or folder rescans,
                              with closed-store receipts
  recordings                  cloud recording assets and verified local archives
  remote-meetings             upcoming Zoom meetings; stored meeting reads
                              remain under meetings
  skill                       the instructions an agent is given for this tool
  serve [options]             serve read-only meeting tools over MCP stdio
  help [command]              display help for command
